# navigation
- label: the Chat home, Runs, run chat and insights pages carry the same section nav — Chat (/), Runs (/sessions), Insights (/insights) — with aria-current on the page you are on
  id: uxnav
  command: grep -q 'export function appNavHtml' src/browser/app-chrome.js && grep -q "nav: 'runs'" src/browser/browser-page-build.js && grep -q "nav: 'chat'" src/browser/run-page.js && grep -q 'appNavHtml("insights")' src/browser/insights-page.js
  tags: [spec, ui-extra-pass, implemented]
- label: g then i jumps to Insights through the CommandPalette's existing g-chord hotkeys (next to g c Chat and g r Runs), and the palette lists Go to Insights
  id: uxgkey
  command: grep -q 'installPageHotkey("tqHotkeyGoI", "g i"' src/browser/command-palette.js && grep -q 'id: "goto-insights"' src/browser/command-palette.js
  tags: [spec, ui-extra-pass, implemented]
- label: the served session viewer (/view, not an exported or shared file) shows a "← Runs" link back to /sessions; compare and route errors return to /sessions, the list the user came from
  id: uxback
  command: grep -q 'data-tq-served' src/routes/route-handlers-pages.js && grep -q "header-back" src/render/render-core-shell.js && grep -q 'href="/sessions">&larr; back to sessions' src/browser/compare-page.js
  tags: [spec, ui-extra-pass, implemented]

# runs list
- label: Runs list and Live rail show encoded project folders without the home prefix and with 8-character UUIDs (prettyProject), keeping the raw value as the title and as the filter value
  id: uxproj
  command: node --input-type=module -e 'import { prettyProject as p } from "./src/filter/filter-formats.js"; const r = p("-Users-me--kandev-tasks-9131a868-bf1c-463a-aa3e-3fdd73fc9c90"); if (r !== "kandev-tasks-9131a868") { console.error(r); process.exit(1); } if (p("zeta") !== "zeta" || p("-home-demo-code-web-dashboard") !== "web-dashboard") process.exit(1);'
  tags: [spec, ui-extra-pass, implemented]
- label: a grade chip explains itself in its title (letter, score out of 100, and what it is computed from)
  id: uxgrade
  command: grep -q "/100 \\\\\\\\u2014 from tool-call error rate" src/browser/browser-client.js
  tags: [spec, ui-extra-pass, implemented]
- label: an empty Runs list says why — "No runs match <filter>" with a Clear filters button, or "No runs recorded yet" with where tracequest looks and a + New run button
  id: uxempty
  command: grep -q 'function emptyStateHtml' src/browser/browser-client.js && grep -q 'No runs recorded yet' src/browser/browser-client.js && grep -q 'data-empty-action="clear"' src/browser/browser-client.js
  tags: [spec, ui-extra-pass, implemented]
- label: harness plan windows render as one scrollable line under the app bar (used % with a meter, reset time; remaining % kept for screen readers) instead of a multi-row uppercase block
  id: uxusage
  command: grep -q 'usage-bar' src/browser/app-chrome.js && grep -q 'flex-wrap: nowrap;' src/browser/app-chrome.js && grep -q 'usage-meter-left' src/browser/app-chrome.js
  tags: [spec, ui-extra-pass, implemented]

# session viewer
- label: the session viewer's errors panel lists the most frequent kinds of failure (identical tool + first output line grouped, with a count, the call that failed and the first chapter), up to 6, each jumping to the first chapter where it happened, plus how many other kinds remain
  id: uxerrs
  command: grep -q "className: 'error-list-item'" src/render/render-ui-errors.js && grep -q 'of failure in the chapters below' src/render/render-ui-errors.js
  tags: [spec, ui-extra-pass, implemented]

# compare
- label: compare opens with one sentence naming which run was longer, more expensive and had more errors, shows B-relative-to-A deltas (×, ÷ or %) on duration, turns, tool calls, cost and tokens, and does not colour differences under 5%
  id: uxcmp
  command: node --input-type=module -e 'import { buildMetricTableHtml as t } from "./src/chapters/compare-metrics.js"; const n = t([["Cache hit","95%","96%","higher",0.95,0.96]]); const c = t([["Cost","$1","$3","lower",1,3]]); if (/delta-(good|bad)/.test(n)) process.exit(1); if (!c.includes("delta-good") || !c.includes("cmp-delta")) process.exit(1);' && node --input-type=module -e 'import { buildCompareVerdictHtml as v } from "./src/chapters/compare-metrics.js"; const t = v({id:"a1",durationMs:60000,cost:1,errors:7},{id:"b2",durationMs:2406000,cost:3.7,errors:21}).replace(/<[^>]+>/g,""); if (t !== "b2 ran 40.1× longer and cost 3.7× more than a1, with 21 errors to its 7.") { console.error(t); process.exit(1); }'
  tags: [spec, ui-extra-pass, implemented]
- label: compare can swap sides with a header link or the s key, and its source badges are the shared sentence-case tinted pill, not uppercase on a solid fill
  id: uxswap
  command: grep -q 'id="cmpSwap"' src/browser/compare-page.js && ! grep -A12 '^\.cmp-source-badge {' src/browser/compare-page-css.js | grep -q 'text-transform: uppercase'
  tags: [spec, ui-extra-pass, implemented]

# theme
- label: every page has a light theme that follows the system by default; the app bar toggle overrides it and is remembered in localStorage (tq-theme); dark stays the default tokens
  id: uxlight
  command: grep -q 'prefers-color-scheme: light' src/browser/shared-css-tokens.js && grep -q 'html\[data-theme="light"\]' src/browser/shared-css-tokens.js && grep -q 'id="themeToggle"' src/browser/app-chrome.js && grep -q 'tq-theme' src/browser/app-chrome.js
  tags: [spec, ui-extra-pass, implemented]
